    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter the June 22nd slate with high offensive expectations, headlined by **Jackson Merrill** (74.59) and **Gunnar Henderson** (67.48). **Jackson Merrill** presents the day's premier opportunity, as he faces a favorable matchup against Holmes, G (R) with a massive +13% platoon edge and the benefit of hitting in the #2 hole. Similarly, **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** (65.57) are poised to exploit the high xERA (5.75) of opposing starter Aldegheri. While **Kyle Tucker** (66.61) remains an elite start, **Andy Pages** (62.80) is an intriguing secondary play; beyond his strong projection, he benefits from a \"Slow SP Delivery\" factor against Matthews, which theoretically increases his stolen base potential\u2014a critical consideration given our strategic emphasis on speed.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved the bench, where **Miguel Vargas** (48.35) narrowly missed the final lineup spot. While his position in the #2 hole provided a strong +8% order bump, he was suppressed by an unfavorable matchup against Williams, G (R) and a defensive penalty related to the opposing catcher's pop time. Consequently, the optimizer favored **Dominic Smith** and **Wade Meckler** to round out the outfield due to better raw efficiency against their respective matchups. We continue to monitor **Nasim Nunez** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, both of whom were held out today as they fell below our 40-point \"Zebras Floor\" against the left-handed Mayza.\n\nInvestors should note that while the weather looks clear, we are tracking the matchup for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.40) closely; despite a positive park factor, his output is currently hampered by an -17% penalty against the skill set of Brown, H (R). We are prioritizing high-upside plays like **Jackson Merrill** and **Gunnar Henderson** to anchor our Roto categories, specifically looking for opportunities where favorable order positioning mitigates the threat of mid-tier opposing arms like King, M and Matthews.",
